From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 11:37:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: jz_sfc: don't touch flash after kfree on probe error

jz_sfc_probe() frees the freshly allocated struct jz_sfc when
mtd_device_parse_register() fails and then reads flash->dev for
dev_set_drvdata(). With SLUB debugging enabled the freed slot is
poisoned with 0x6b, so the CPU takes an unhandled unaligned access at
0x6b6b6b6f instead of the driver failing cleanly:

  mtd: partition size too small (0)
  $ 4 : 6b6b6b6b ...
  BadVA : 6b6b6b6f
  epc   : 801e118c dev_set_drvdata+0x4
  ra    : 8042ad80 jz_sfc_probe+0x634

dev_set_drvdata(flash->dev, NULL) is just platform_set_drvdata(pdev,
NULL) here, so clear the driver data before the free.

The reported trigger is an 8MB SPI-NOR camera whose rootfs grew to fill
the whole flash, leaving the generated command line as
"...6144k(rootfs),0k(data),8192k@0(all)". cmdlinepart rejects any
partition smaller than a page, which is what makes
mtd_device_parse_register() return -EINVAL in the first place.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
 drivers/mtd/devices/jz_sfc.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mtd/devices/jz_sfc.c b/drivers/mtd/devices/jz_sfc.c
--- a/drivers/mtd/devices/jz_sfc.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/devices/jz_sfc.c
@@ -1247,8 +1247,9 @@
 
 	ret = mtd_device_parse_register(&flash->mtd, NULL , NULL, NULL, 0);
 	if (ret) {
-		kfree(flash);
+		/* flash->dev is &pdev->dev: clear the drvdata before freeing */
 		dev_set_drvdata(flash->dev, NULL);
+		kfree(flash);
 		return -ENODEV;
 	}
 	printk("SPI NOR MTD LOAD OK\n");
-- 
2.34.1

